.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt DMESG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dmesg
.Nd print the kernel boot log
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command prints
.Pa /dev/bootlog ,
which the kernel fills as it starts.
Root may also read the log with any program that reads a file.
.Pp
.Nm
accepts no arguments.
Linux's options apply to a ring buffer that this kernel does not keep.
Arguments are refused rather than ignored.
The BusyBox dmesg applet is not built because it cannot read this kernel's log.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/bootlog
.It Pa /bin/dmesg
Script installed on os-real, metal, and recovery images.
.It Pa /dev/bootlog
Kernel boot log, readable by root.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
An invocation with any argument exits with status 1.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
An argument produces:
.Dl dmesg: this machine's boot log is /dev/bootlog and takes no options
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bootlog 4 ,
.Xr rach2 7
